{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774201223,"nonce":"HVztJI/kCAV07OdNn+EjwUROGXs=","title":"Convention: fixes must not regress previously requested features still in conversation context","message":"When fixing one issue, agents must not regress features requested earlier in the same conversation. If the user asked for metadata + icons on hover overlays, and then asks for a different fix, the metadata + icons must not disappear.\n\nThis applies when the prior request is still in the agents context window. Stale requests (from prior sessions) may be superseded, but anything in the current conversation is assumed to be desired unless explicitly contradicted.\n\nProposed CLAUDE.md addition under Hard Constraints or Proactive Behaviors:\n\"When implementing fixes or new features, verify that previously requested changes from the current conversation are preserved. Do not regress features the user asked for in this session. Before committing, review the conversation for features that were implemented in prior commits and confirm they still work.\"","files":null}]}